$DATUM Quinazoline-2,4(1H,3H)-dione (23). The mixture of anthranilic acid (500
mg, 3.65 mmol) and urea (2.2 g, mol) was heated at 150 °C for 6 h. The
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature and then water (50 mL)
was added to quench the reaction. The crude product was obtained by
filtration and then washed with water (20 mL × 3). The residue was
dissolved in hot aqueous NaOH and cooled to 0 °C, and pH was adjusted to
5-6 using dilute HCl and stirred for 30 min. The crude mixture was
filtered and washed with water and dried under vacuum. Compound 23 as
white solid (500 mg, 85%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6 ) δ 11.28 (s, 1H),
11.14 (s, 1H), 7.88 (dd, J = 7.8, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 7.65-7.60 (m, 1H), 7.17
(ddd, J = 8.2, 6.1, 1.8 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, DMSO-d6 ) δ 162.9,
150.3, 140.9, 135.0, 127.0, 122.4, 115.3, 114.4. MS (ESI-TOF, m/z):
calculated for C8H6N2O2 [M + H]+ 163.0502; found 163.0491.
