$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Symmetrical Urea Synthesis A stainless steel
autoclave (50 mL) was charged with complex 1 (0.01 mmol, 5.9 mg), amine
(2 mmol), methanol (2 mmol, 81 µL), and toluene (1.5 mL) in an
argon-filled glove box. The vessel was heated to 140°C (bath temperature)
under closed conditions. After 24 h, the reaction was cooled to 0°C for
30 min. The generated H2 was carefully released in a fumehood. n-Hexane
(40 mL) was then added to the reaction mixture. The resulting solid was
collected and further washed with cold diethyl ether to afford the
corresponding product. 1,3-dibenzylurea White solid (223.9 mg 0.933 mmol,
93%). The compound was identified by spectral comparison with literature
data.3 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6, δ): 4.23 (s, 4H, 2CH2), 6.45 (br, 2H,
2NH), 7.20-7.34 (m, 10H, 10CH) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, alternative preparation shown, autoclave used, NMR yield
reported - 93% isolated yield, trace of formamide, optimization study
(ruthenium catalyst, catalyst loading, use of base, solvent,
stoichiometry, concentration), scalable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ruthenium-Catalyzed Urea Synthesis Using Methanol as the C1 Source
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
