$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Benzoxazolone N-Carboxamides 53,
55-61, 64, 65 via Method C (Scheme 6, Table 3). In an oven-dried flask,
triphosgene (1.0 equiv) was dissolved in dry DCM (5 mL per mmol
triphosgene). A solution of 3H-1,3-benzoxazol-2-one (50, 1.0 equiv) and
Et3N (4.0 equiv) in dry DCM (5.6 mL per mmol of 50) was added at 0 °C,
and the reaction was stirred for 1 h at rt under nitrogen. Then a
solution of the appropriate amine (1.5 equiv) and Et3N (1.5 equiv) in dry
DCM (6.5 mL per mmol of amine) was added at 0 °C, and the reaction was
stirred at rt for 3 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with DCM (20 mL
per mmol of 50) and quenched with sat aq NH4Cl (30 mL per mmol of 50).
The two phases were separated and the aq layer was extracted with DCM (3
× 20 mL per mmol of 50). The combined organic phases were dried over
Na2SO4, evaporated on Celite or silica, and the compound was purified by
silica gel column chromatography using the Teledyne ISCO apparatus
(cyclohexane/EtOAc). 2-Oxo-N-(phenethyl)-1,3-benzoxazole-3-carboxamide
(53). The reaction was carried out following method C, using 50 (60 mg,
0.444 mmol) and 2-phenylethan-1-amine 67k (80 mg, 0.084 mL, 0.660 mmol).
White solid (79 mg, 64%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.96 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
2H), 3.69 (td, J = 5.8, 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.19-7.29 (m, 6H), 7.34 (dd, J =
5.8, 8.9 Hz, 2H), 8.05-8.09 (m, 1H), 8.09-8.17 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (101 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 35.9, 41.8, 110.0, 115.7, 124.7, 125.1, 126.9, 128.1, 128.9,
128.9, 138.4, 141.9, 149.9, 153.2. MS (ESI) m/z: 283 [M + H]+, 300 [M +
NH4]+. MS (ESI) m/z: 281 [M -H]-.
