$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Benzoxazolone N-Carboxamides 53, 55-61, 64, 65 via Method C (Scheme 6,
Table 3). In an oven-dried flask, triphosgene (1.0 equiv) was dissolved
in dry DCM (5 mL per mmol triphosgene). A solution of
3H-1,3-benzoxazol-2-one (50, 1.0 equiv) and Et3N (4.0 equiv) in dry DCM
(5.6 mL per mmol of 50) was added at 0 °C, and the reaction was stirred
for 1 h at rt under nitrogen. Then a solution of the appropriate amine
(1.5 equiv) and Et3N (1.5 equiv) in dry DCM (6.5 mL per mmol of amine)
was added at 0 °C, and the reaction was stirred at rt for 3 h. The
reaction mixture was diluted with DCM (20 mL per mmol of 50) and quenched
with sat aq NH4Cl (30 mL per mmol of 50). The two phases were separated
and the aq layer was extracted with DCM (3 × 20 mL per mmol of 50). The
combined organic phases were dried over Na2SO4, evaporated on Celite or
silica, and the compound was purified by silica gel column chromatography
using the Teledyne ISCO apparatus (cyclohexane/EtOAc).
2-Oxo-N-(phenethyl)-1,3-benzoxazole-3-carboxamide (53). The reaction was
carried out following method C, using 50 (60 mg, 0.444 mmol) and
2-phenylethan-1-amine 67k (80 mg, 0.084 mL, 0.660 mmol).
N-[4-(2-Naphthyl)butyl]-2-oxo-1,3-benzoxazole-3-carboxamide (57). The
reaction was carried out following method C, using 50 (26 mg, 0.190 mmol)
and amine 67a (68 mg, 0.300 mmol). White solid (36 mg, 52%). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.66-1.79 (m, 2H), 1.78-1.91 (m, 2H), 2.84 (t, J = 7.4 Hz,
2H), 3.47 (td, J = 7.0, 5.7 Hz, 2H), 7.21-7.30 (m, 3H), 7.34 (dd, J =
8.4, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.38-7.49 (m, 2H), 7.60-7.66 (m, 1H), 7.74-7.84 (m,
3H), 8.01-8.12 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 28.5, 29.2, 35.7,
40.2, 110.1, 115.7, 124.6, 125.1, 125.3, 126.0, 126.6, 127.3, 127.5,
127.7, 128.1, 128.1, 132.2, 133.7, 139.5, 141.9, 150.0, 153.3. MS (ESI)
m/z: nonionizable compound under routine conditions used.
