concentrated in vacuo. The crude phenyl carbamate was used either
directly in the subsequent step or following purification by flash silica
chromatography. A solution of the phenyl carbamate (1 equiv), the
appropriate amine (2-5 equiv), and triethylamine (3.25 equiv) in either
NMP or DMF was heated between 50 and 70 °C for 2 h or until complete by
TLC or LCMS analysis. The reaction mixture was purified by either flash
column chromatography or HPLC.
