$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure N, N’-carbonyldiimidazole
(165 mg, 1.02 mmol, 1.1 equiv) was dissolved in anhydrous THF, a solution
of 9-amino(9-deoxy)epiquine or 9-amino(9-deoxy)epiquinine (300 mg, 0.93
mmol, 1equiv) in THF (5 ml) was added dropwise in 1 h, the reaction
mixture was stirred for another 1 h. Then aminoalcohol (1.1 equiv) and
triethylamine (142ul, 1.1 equiv) were added in one portion respectively,
the resulting mixture was stirred until TLC showed that the reaction was
completed. The mixture was diluted with 36 ml ethylacetate, then washed
with water (10×15ml), the organic phase was dried over Na2SO4. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the crude product was
purified by flash chromatography (ethylacetate/MeOH=10:1). Urea 2a
derived from quinine and (1S, 2R)-1-Amino-2-indanol Urea 2d derived from
quinine and (1S, 2R)-2-Amino-1, 2-diphenylethanol Light yellow solid, 282
mg, 54% yield. m.p. =116-118°C, [a]D 25 = -81.3 (c = 0.3, CHCl3). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.67 (d, J = 4.5 Hz, 1H), 8.01 (d, J = 9.2 Hz, 1H),
7.64 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (dd, J = 9.2, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 7.24-7.04 (m,
7H), 6.96-6.86 (m, 2H), 6.81 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 2H), 6.32 (s, 1H), 5.76-5.48
(m, 2H), 5.22 (br.s, 1H), 5.06-4.86 (m, 4H), 4.21 (br.s, 1H), 3.92 (s,
3H), 3.30-3.00 (m, 3H), 2.81-2.52 (m, 2H), 2.28 (br.s, 1H), 1.75-1.51 (m,
3H), 1.49-1.33 (m, 1H), 1.03-0.83 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ
157.99, 147.55, 144.64, 140.93, 140.45, 138.23, 131.62, 127.86, 127.75,
127.63, 127.45, 127.26, 126.82, 121.84, 114.80, 101.94, 71.83, 69.30,
64.40, 60.54, 55.70, 55.61, 40.81, 39.17, 27.58, 27.28, 25.86. HRMS
(ESI): calculated for C35H39N4O3 [M+H]+: 563.3017, found 563.3014.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Phase-Transfer Catalysts Bearing Multiple Hydrogen-Bonding
Donors: Highly Efficient Catalysts for Enantio- and Diastereoselective
Nitro-Mannich Reaction of Amidosulfones
