$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-Phenylsemicarbazide (Y) 4-Phenylsemicarbazide was prepared by reacting
phenyl urea (0.13 g, 1 mmol) with hydrazine hydrate (1.5 ml, 3 mmol) in
the presence of NaOH (0.04 g, 1 mmol) in ethanol under reflux for 48 h
with stirring. The resultant product was filtered, washed with cold water
and dried. The dried product was recrystallized from warm water and dried
at room temperature. The completion of reaction was monitored by running
TLC. Yield, 89 %; Mp 116-118°C. IR (KBr) υmax/cm-1 3,436 (-NH), 1,676
(C=O), 1,584 (C=C). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6 ); δ: 9.16 (s, 1H, NHNH2),
8.04 (s, 1H, Ar-NH), 7.11-7.66 (m, 5H, Ar-H), 6.57 (s, 2H, NH2). LCMS
m/z; 152.1, [M+2]+. Anal. Calcd for C7H9N3O (%): C, 55.62; H, 6.00; N,
27.80. Found: C, 55.54; H, 5.92; N, 27.93.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
