$DATUM 1-(3-(2-Ethylpyridin-3-yloxy)-5-(pyridin-2-ylthio)pyridin-2-yl)-3-methylurea
(16a). 3-(2-Ethylpyridin-3-yloxy)-5-(pyridin-2-ylthio)pyridin-2-amine
(200 mg, 0.617 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (3 mL) and pyridine (149 μL,
1.85 mmol) and 4-nitrophenyl carbonochloridate (261 mg, 1.29 mmol) were
added and the reaction stirred at room temperature for 1 hour. 33% Methyl
amine in EtOH (774 μL, 6.17 mmol) was added and stirred at room
temperature for 3 hours. Excess K2CO3 and EtOH (2 mL) was added and
stirred at room temperature overnight. The reaction was partitioned
between water and CH2Cl2, extracted twice, dried over sodium sulfate,
filtered and concentrated. The residue was purified over silica gel (5%
MeOH in EtOAc).
1-(3-(2-ethylpyridin-3-yloxy)-5-(pyridin-2-ylthio)pyridin-2-yl)-3-methylurea
(125 mg, 0.328 mmol, 53.2% yield) as a white solid. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm
9.17 (m, 1H), 8.45 (m, 1H), 8.32 (m, 1H), 8.09 (m, 1H), 7.58 (s, 1H),
7.48 (m, 1H), 7.27 (m, 1H), 7.18 (dd, J = 8.0, 4.5 Hz, 1H), 7.03-6.95 (m,
3H), 3.01 (d, J = 4.7 Hz, 3H), 2.79 (q, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 1.25 (t, J = 7.6
Hz, 3H); MS (APCI) m/e 382.1 (M+H)+.
