$DATUM (R)-1-(7-Fluoro-2,2-dimethylchroman-4-yl)-3-(1-methy1H-indazo4-yl)urea
(34). A mixture of DSC (0.811 g, 3.17 mmol), acetonitrile (10 mL),
pyridine (0.233 mL, 2.88 mmol), and 1-methy1H-indazo4-amine43 (0.466 g,
3.17 mmol) was stirred at ambient temperature. After 10 min,
N,N-diisopropylethylamine (1.494 mL, 8.64 mmol) and
(R)-7-fluoro-2,2-dimethylchroman-4-aminium
(R)-2-hydroxy-2-phenylacetate29 (1.00 g, 2.88 mmol) were added. After 10
min, the reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc (50 mL) and washed with
2N NaOH (20 mL x 2), water (20 mL), 2 N HCl (20 mL x 2), and brine (10
mL) and dried (Na2SO4). The organic phase was concentrated and the
residue was purified by silica gel chromatography (gradient elution,
25-75% EtOAc/hexanes) to give N-methylindazole urea 34. Yield (780 mg,
2.12 mmol, 74%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 8.74 (s, 1H), 8.04 (s, 1H),
7.71 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.37-7.25 (m, 2H), 7.17 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H),
6.76 (dd, J = 8.6, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 6.72 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 6.61 (dd, J =
10.6, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 5.03-4.93 (m, 1H), 4.01 (s, 3H), 2.20 (dd, J = 13.3,
6.1 Hz, 1H), 2.00-1.73 (m, 1H), 1.42 (s, 3H), 1.31 (s, 3H). MS (DCI/NH3)
m/z 369 (M + H)+; [α]23 D +11.0° (c 0.61, CH3OH).
