$DATUM Experimental Procedures. Procedure for Isoquinoline Urea Preparation
(General Procedure A). (R)-1-(6-Fluoro-2,2-dimethylchroman-
4-yl)-3-(isoquinolin-5-yl)urea (4). A solution of N,N'-disuccinimidyl
carbonate (DSC, 1.38 g, 5.38 mmol), pyridine (0.435 mL, 5.38 mmol), and
isoquinolin-5-amine (0.738 g, 5.12 mmol) in acetonitrile (15 mL) was
stirred at ambient temperature for 30 min.
(R)-6-Fluoro-2,2-dimethylchroman-4-aminium
(R)-2-hydroxy-2-phenylacetate29 (1.78 g, 5.12 mmol) (or other
corresponding substituted chromanamine salts for subsequent isoquinoline
ureas prepared via this general procedure) and N,N-diisopropylethylamine
(2.66 mL, 15.4 mmol) were added. The reaction was stirred for 90 min and
concentrated. The residue was diluted with EtOAc (300 mL), washed with
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (100 mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and
concentrated. The residue was purified by silica gel chromatography
(gradient elution, 0-10% MeOH/CH2Cl2) to give isoquinoline urea 4. White
solid, yield (1.12 g, 3.07 mmol, 60%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 9.29
(d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H), 8.76 (s, 1H), 8.56 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 8.34 (dd, J
=J =7.7, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 7.94 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 1H), 7.77 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H),
7.64 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.12 (ddd, J = 9.4, 3.2, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 7.06-6.98
(m, 2H), 6.79 (dd, J = 8.9, 4.9 Hz, 1H), 5.05-4.95 (m, 1H), 2.21 (dd, J =
13.2, 6.2 Hz, 1H), 1.78 (dd, J = 13.2, 10.9 Hz, 1H), 1.41 (s, 3H), 1.29
(s, 3H). MS (DCI/NH3) m/z 366 (M + H)+; [α]23 D +32.6° (c 0.65, CH3OH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
(R)-1-(7-Chloro-2,2-bis(fluoromethyl)chroman-4-yl)-3-(3-methylisoquinolin-5-yl)urea
(A-1165442): A Temperature-Neutral Transient Receptor Potential
Vanilloid-1 (TRPV1) Antagonist with Analgesic Efficacy
