$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Corresponding amine (1 equiv.) and
triethylamine (1.2 equiv.) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (54 mM corresponding
to amine) and stirred at -78 °C. Triphosgene (0.37 equiv.) dissolved in
CH2Cl2 (20 mM, corresponding triphosgene) was added dropwise at -78 °C.
The reaction was then warm to rt and was stirred for 30 min. The reaction
was cooled to 0 °C. Corresponding piperidine (1.1 equiv.) dissolved in
CH2Cl2 (54 mM, corresponding piperidine) was added slowly and the
reaction was further stirred at rt for 12 h. The reaction was quenched
with the addition of HCl solution (2M). The organic layer was collected
and the aqueous layer was further extracted with EtOAc (EtOAc: Aqueous
layer/1:1) for three times. The combined organic layer was washed with
sat. NaCl solution. The organic layer was dried over anhydrous magnesium
sulfate and was concentrated in vacuo. The product was purified by flash
chromatography. The synthesis was carried out according to synthetic
pathway 3. Piperidine E (50 mg, 271.7 μmol) was reacted with
4-(perfluoropropan-2-yl)aniline (78 mg, 299 μmol). The product was
purified by flash chromatography (EtOAc: Hexane/8:2). The product 13 was
further purified by crystallization (MeOH with water). The synthesis was
carried out according to synthetic pathway 3. Piperidine E (50 mg, 271.7
μmol) was reacted with trans-4-ethylcyclohexanamine (38 mg, 299 μmol).
The product 17 was eluted by flash chromatography with EtOAc. The product
1-(trans-4-ethylcyclohexyl)-3-(1-(2-methylbutanoyl)piperidin-4-yl)urea
(17) was further purified by crystallization (EtOAc in Hexane). Yield: 57
mg, 62%. Purity (NMR): ≥95%. 1H NMR (d6-DMSO, 300 Mhz): ∂ 5.72 (br, 1H),
5.55 (t, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 4.17 (br, 1H), 3.83 (d, J = 12 Hz, 1H), 3.5-3.7
(m, 1H), 3.2-3.4 (m, 1H), 3.10 (t, J = 12 Hz, 1H), 2.6-2.8 (m, 2H), 1.79
(d, J = 12 Hz, 3H), 1.69 (d, J = 12 Hz, 3H), 1.4-1.6 (m, 2H), 1.2-1.3 (m,
2H), 1.1-1.2 (m, 2H), 0.7-1.1 (m, 16H) HRMS (calculated for [H+]:
C19H36N3O2): 338.2802 ; found (ESI(+), [M-H+]): 324.2834 Melting point
(°C): 149.8-150.8 (150.4).
