$DATUM 3-(5-Chloro-[1,3]thiazolo[5,4-b]pyridin-2-yl)-1-(2-{1′-(2,2-dimethylpropyl)-5-fluoro-4-(4-fluorophenyl)-7-methoxy-1,2-dihydrospiro[indole-3,4′-piperidine]-1-yl}phenyl)urea
(19c). To a solutionof 18b (858mg, 1.745mmol) and K2CO3 (482 mg,
3.49mmol) in DCE (15 mL) was added 4-nitrophenyl chloroformate (387 mg,
1.920 mmol) portionwise, and the solution was stirred for 1 h at rt.
5-Chlorothiazolo[5,4-b]pyridin-2-amine (486 mg, 2.62 mmol) and DMAP (213
mg, 1.745 mmol) were added, and the mixture was stirred at 75 °C for 4.5
h. The reaction was diluted with DCM and washed with 1 N NaOH (30 mL × 2)
and brine consecutively. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4,
concentrated, and purified by flash chromatography, eluted with
EtOAc/hexanes. 19c as a pale yellow solid (981 mg, 80% yield). LCMS (ESI)
m/z 703.5 (M + H)+. 1H NMR (400 MHz, chloroform-d) δ 8.04 (br s, 1H),
7.44 (br s, 1H), 7.35-7.27 (m, 1H), 7.22 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 7.16-7.03
(m, 5H), 6.58 (d, J = 10.9 Hz, 1H), 3.81 (d, J = 10.4 Hz, 1H), 3.56 (s,
3H), 3.26 (d, J = 10.1 Hz, 1H), 2.36 (t, J = 13.0 Hz, 2H), 2.10-1.93 (m,
2H), 1.82-1.70 (m, 2H), 1.65-1.58 (m, 1H), 1.39-1.11 (m, 3H), 0.63 (s,
9H).
