$DATUM 2-Chloro-5-ethoxy-N-(6-(3-(4-methylpiperazin-1-yl)propylsulfonyl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-ylcarbamoyl)benzamide
(19) 2-Chloro-5-ethoxybenzamide (250 mg, 1.25 mmol) and oxalyl chloride
(0.109 mL, 1.25 mmol) were suspended in THF (15 mL) and sealed into a
microwave tube. The reaction was heated to 120°C for 5 min in a microwave
reactor and cooled to rt. The vial was cautiously degassed and opened. 51
(431 mg, 1.13 mmol) was added portionwise and the suspension was stirred
at 120°C in a microwave for a further 5 min. The vial was cooled to rt
and cautiously degassed. 1-Methylpiperazine (0.417 mL, 3.76 mmol) was
added portionwise and the resulting suspension stirred at rt for 16 h.
The reaction mixture was evaporated to dryness and purified by flash
silica chromatography, elution gradient (1-15% MeOH in DCM). The title
compound as a beige solid (428 mg, 59%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) 1.41
(3H, t), 1.76-1.84 (2H, m), 2.45-2.51 (9H, m), 2.71 (4H, s), 3.40-3.45
(2H, m), 4.13-4.18 (2H, m), 7.18-7.20 (1H, m), 7.31 (1H, d), 7.54 (1H,
d), 7.97-8.06 (2H, m), 8.72 (1H, d), 11.21 (2H, br s); m/z MH+ = 580.
HRMS (ES+) for C25H30ClN5O5S2 (MH+): calcd, 580.1450; found 580.1452.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (stages 1-2), sealed microwave vial used
