$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Cu-Catalyzed Intramolecular C-H/N-H Coupling
of 2-Aminobiphenyls 1 Synthesis of 2a: Cu(OAc)2 (14 mg, 0.075 mmol),
N-{(1,1’-biphenyl)-2-yl}picolinamide (1a, 69 mg, 0.25 mmol), acetic acid
(15 mg, 0.25 mmol), manganese dioxide (43 mg, 0.50 mmol), and
N,N-dimethylformamide (DMF, 1.5 mL) were placed in a 2 mL microwave
vessel. The vessel was sealed with a cap and the mixture was irradiated
under microwave reactor conditions at 200°C for 1 h. The resulting
mixture was then quenched with water and ethylenediamine (ca. 1 mL). The
mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate, and the combined organic layer
was dried over sodium sulfate. Concentration in vacuo followed by silica
gel column purification with hexane/ethyl acetate (5:1, v/v).
9H-carbazole (2a, 40 mg, 0.24 mmol) in 96% yield. Entry: 10; 2a; Yield
80%; N-Carbamoylcarbazole 2a-CONMe2 . 9H-Carbazole (2a) m.p.
243.0-244.0°C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 7.15 (ddd, J = 0.8, 7.2, 8.0
Hz, 2H), 7.38 (ddd, J = 0.8, 7.2, 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.48 (td, J = 0.8, 8.0 Hz,
2H), 8.10 (td, J = 0.8, 8.0 Hz, 2H), 11.22 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
DMSO-d 6) δ 110.87, 118.41, 120.08, 122.33, 125.43, 139.66; HRMS (EI) m/z
(M+) calcd for C12H9N: 167.0735, found: 167.0733.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM intramolecular coupling, alternative reaction conditions shown, sealed
tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Carbazoles by Copper-Catalyzed Intramolecular C-H/N-H
Coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
