$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The synthesis of 3’a To a solution of 2-(tritylthio)ethylamine (C2 linker
unit) (240 mg, 0.676 mmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (2 mL) were added 1,
1’-carbonyldiimidazole (166 mg, 1.01 mmol) and Et3N (160 µL, 1.15 mmol)
under Ar atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred at 40 0 C for 4 h,
and the G-clamp unit was added to the mixture. After 5 h at 40 0 C, satd
NaHCO3 aq (3 mL) was added and the mixture was stirred for overnight. The
mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (25 mL) and the organic layer was
washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated in vacuo. The
resulting residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography
