$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The synthesis of 3’a To a solution of
2-(tritylthio)ethylamine (C2 linker unit) (240 mg, 0.676 mmol) in
anhydrous CH2Cl2 (2 mL) were added 1, 1’-carbonyldiimidazole (166 mg,
1.01 mmol) and Et3N (160 µL, 1.15 mmol) under Ar atmosphere. The reaction
mixture was stirred at 40 0 C for 4 h, and the G-clamp unit was added to
the mixture. After 5 h at 40 0 C, satd NaHCO3 aq (3 mL) was added and the
mixture was stirred for overnight. The mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2
(25 mL) and the organic layer was washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4
and evaporated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
column chromatography (CHCl3/acetone =4:1). The synthesis of 3’b 3’b was
synthesized by a similar procedure as described for the synthesis of 3’a
except that 3-(tritylthio)propylamine (C3 linker unit) was used instead
of 2-(tritylthio)ethyl-amine. A pale yellow foam (78 %). 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CD3OD) δ (ppm) 7.63 (1H, s), 7.34 (6H, d, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.23 (6H, t, J =
7.4 Hz), 7.16 (3H, t, J = 7.4 Hz), 6.83 (1H, t, J = 8.4 Hz), 6.61 (1H, d,
J = 8.0 Hz), 6.37 (1H, d, J = 8.4 Hz), 6.18 (1H, t, J = 6.0 Hz),
4.47-4.46 (1H, m), 4.02 (2H, t, J = 5.0 Hz), 3.95-3.93 (2H,m), 3.83 (1H,
dd, J = 12, 3.2 Hz), 3.51 (2H, t, J = 5.2 Hz), 3.03 (2H, t, J = 6.8 Hz),
2.34-2.29 (1H, m), 2.17-2.06 (3H, m), 1.49 (2H, quint, J = 6.8 Hz), 0.97
(9H, s), 0.91 (9H, s), 0.18 (3H, s), 0.16 (3H, s), 0.10 (6H, s). IR
(cm-1): 2927, 1672, 1558. HR ESI-MS (m/z): Calcd. for 964.4529 ([M+H]+ ),
found 964.4561.
