$DATUM 1-[(1R,2R)-2-(Dimethylamino)cyclohexyl]-3-(2-ethynylphenyl)-urea (4). To
a solution of triphosgen (2.2 mmol, 630 mg) in THF (10 mL) was added a
solution of 2 (4.3 mmol, 500 mg) and NEt3 (17 mmol, 1.72 g) in THF (10
mL) dropwise at 0 °C. After being stirred at room temperature for 1 h,
the mixture was filtrated through a pad of Celite, and the filtrate was
concentrated in vacuo to give the crude isocyanate, which was then
dissolved in THF (10 mL). To this solution was added
(1R,2R)-N1,N1-dimethylcyclohexane-1,2-diamine (505 mg, 3.6 mmol), and the
resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature for 5 h. The mixture
was then concentrated in vacuo to afford a crude product, which was
purified by silica gel chromatography (CHCl3/MeOH = 10:1) to give 4.
White solid, yield 981 mg, 80%. mp 137-138 °C; [α] 25 D -17.8 (c 2.30,
CHCl3); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.18 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (d, J = 7.7 Hz,
1H), 7.29 (br, 1H), 7.29 (dd, J = 7.7, 7.7 Hz, 1H), 6.90 (dd, J = 7.7,
7.7 Hz, 1H), 6.09 (br, 1H), 3.51 (s, 1H) 3.50 (m, 1H), 2.46 (m, 2H), 2.32
(s, 6H), 1.83-1.90 (m, 2H), 1.69-1.70 (m, 1H), 1.15-1.36 (m, 4H) ppm; 13C
NMR (CHCl3) δ 155.3, 141.2, 132.2, 130.1, 121.4, 118.4, 109.7, 83.8,
79.9, 66.3, 52.0, 39.9, 33.3, 25.3, 24.6, 21.1 ppm; IR (ATR) 3304, 2930,
1649 cm-1; MS (FAB) 286 (MH+, 100); HRMS (ESI) calcd for C17H24N3O (MH+)
286.1914, found 286.1908.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety (triphosgene in stage 1), dropwise addition of Et3N/THF (stage 1);
isocyanate isolated in stage 1 used crude in stage 2
