$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Synthesis Procedure of the Hosts.
Amino porphyrin and 4 equiv of Et3N were dissolved in dry dichloromethane
(DCM). Then, 1.2 mol equiv of triphosgene was added, and the mixture was
stirred for 0.5 h at room temperature. After the amino porphyrin was
completely consumed, a solution of the corresponding amine and Et3N (2.0
equiv) in dry DCM was dropped slowly into the reaction mixture. The
mixture was stirred vigorously for 5 h at room temperature. The solvent
was removed under vacuum, and the residue was purified by silica gel
column chromatography with DCM/ methanol (20:1) as eluent. The porphyrin
host was obtained as a purple solid by recrystallization from
chloroform/methanol. Synthesis of DP2 2. DP2 2 was prepared according to
the general synthesis procedure. Step 1:
5-(4-aminophenyl)-10,15,20-trisphenylporphyrin (30 mg, 0.048 mmol), Et3N
(28 μL, 0.20 mmol), and triphosgene (17.8 mg, 0.06 mmol); step 2:
N'-Boc-2,2'-diaminodiethylamine (5.1 mg, 0.025 mmol) and Et3N (14 μL,
0.10 mmol). Column chromatography separation and recrystallization afford
a purple solid DP2 2: 35 mg, yield 88%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ
9.07-9.08 (m, 2H), 8.93-8.86 (m, 4H), 8.85-8.74 (m, 12H), 8.25-8.16 (m,
8H), 8.14 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 4H), 8.07 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 4H), 7.90 (d, J = 8.3
Hz, 2H), 7.84-7.72 (m, 18H), 6.58-6.41 (m, 4H), 3.50-3.41 (m, 4H), 1.52
(s, 3H), 1.45 (s, 6H), -2.93 (s, 4H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 142.3,
142.1, 135.4, 134.7, 134.5, 131.3, 127.8, 127.6, 126.8, 126.6, 120.2,
117.9, 46.0, 29.9, 28.6, 28.2, 8.7. HRMS (ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for
C99H80N13O4, 1515.6482; found, 1515.6459.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM amine/TEA/DCM added slowly stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Clawlike Tripodal Porphyrin Trimer: Ion-Controlled On-Off Fullerene
Binding
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fang, Xiang; Zhu, Yi-Zhou; Zheng, Jian-Yu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(3), 1184-1191

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME321 STEP1
$RXN



