$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure 5: Reaction of
3-picolylamine (IId) with 4-nitrophenyl chloroformate followed by
reaction with amines Va-f,n,m,j to yield ureas 38, 41, 44-50.
3-Picolylamine (IId) (1.0 eq.) was dissolved in EtOAc, DIEA (1.2 eq.) was
added, the mixture was cooled on an ice bath and 4-nitrophenyl
chloroformate (1.1 eq.) was added with stirring. After 4 h (or
consumption of the amine IId) the reaction mixture was washed
successively with 5% Na2CO3 (twice), H2O, brine, dried over Mg2SO4,
filtered and concentrated. The resulting 4-nitrophenyl carbamate (1.0
eq.) was dissolved in DMF, amine Va-f,n,m,j (1.0 eq.) was added followed
by HOBt (2.0 eq) and DIEA (0.5 eq.), and heated at 40°C overnight. The
mixture was concentrated and purified by chromatography
(chloroform:methanol:NH3 (25% aq.) 98:2:0.2 to 96:4:0.4) Urea 38, 41, or
44-50.
N-Cyclohexyl-N-(2-morpholinoethoxy)-7-(3-(pyridin-3-ylmethyl)ureido)heptanamide
(38)
N-Cyclopentyl-N-(2-morpholinoethoxy)-6-(3-(pyridin-3-yl)methyl)ureido)hexane-1-sulfonamide
(46) Preparation of 46 was performed according to general procedure 5
using 3-picolylamine (IId) and compound Vd. Yield 80%. 1H-NMR (300 MHz,
CD3OD) δ 8.48 (d, 1H), 8.41 (dd, 1H), 7.78 (dt, 1H), 7.40 (m, 1H), 4.35
(s, 2H), 4.19 (bs, 2H), 4.02 (m, 1H), 3.68 (t, 4H), 3.18 (bs, 2H), 3.14
(t, 2H), 2.63 (t, 2H), 2.52 (t, 4H), 2.0-1.3 (m, 16H). HRMS m/z calcd for
C24H42N5O5S [M+H]+, 512.2907; found, 512.2856.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
