$DATUM N-Cyclohexyl-N-(2-morpholinoethoxy)-6-(3-(pyridin-4-yl)ureido)hexane-1-sulfonamide
oxalate (37) To a solution of 4-aminopyridine (IIa) (0.084 g, 0.89 mmol)
in tetrahydrofuran (3 ml) was added 1,1-carbonyldiimidazole (0.15 g, 0.92
mmol) and the mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. To this
solution 6-amino-N-cyclohexyl-N-(2-morpholinoethoxy)-1-hexanesulfonamide
(Ve) (0.32 g, 0.82 mmol) was added and the mixture was stirred overnight.
The reaction mixture was evaporated and the residue was chromatographed
on silica gel (100 g) with acetonitrile-water-acetic acid (3:1:1) as
eluent. The title compound 37 (0.31 g, 74%) as an oil. The 1H NMR
analysis of the product revealed the presence of imidazole. The product
was purified by reversed phase LC with 0.1% formic acid-acetonitrile
(gradient from 10:90 to 90:10) as eluent to give compound 37 (0.175 g,
42%) as an oil. The obtained oil (0.17 g, 0.33 mmol) was dissolved in
acetonitrile (3 ml) and a solution of oxalic acid (0.03 g, 0.33 mmol) in
acetonitrile (2 ml) was added with stirring. The resulting mixture was
stirred at room temperature until the precipitate formed. The precipitate
was filtered, washed with acetonitrile, and dried in vacuo. The title
compound 37 in a form of oxalate (0.16 g, 30%) as a crystalline solid. An
approximate ratio of the oxalic acid in the product was assessed by
elemental analysis. Mp 129-131°C. 1H NMR (200 MHz, (CD3)2SO) δ 0.91-1.64
(m, 13H), 1.64-2.00 (m, 5H), 2.59-2.80 (m, 4H), 2.97-3.35 (m, 4H),
3.40-3.70 (m, 3H, overlapped with water), 3.92-4.40 (m, overlapped with
water, 6H), 6.78-7.23 (m, 1H), 7.56 (b s, 2H); 8.36 (b s, 2H); 9.50-10.25
(br s, 1H). LCMS (ESI) m/z: 512 [M+H]+. HRMS m/z calcd for C24H42N5O5S
[M+H]+, 512.2907; found, 512.2856. Anal. Calcd for C24H41N5O5S ∙ 1.5
(COOH)2: C, 50.14; H, 6.86; N, 10.83. Found: C, 49.68; H, 6.88; N, 11.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product further converted into oxalate salt
