$DATUM 1,3-Bis(3,6-di-tert-butyl-8-(tert-butoxycarbonylamino)-9H-carbazol-1-yl)urea
(7). CDI (120 mg, 0.74 mmol) and 6 (400 mg, 0.98 mmol) were dissolved in
dry DMF (30 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere, and the mixture was stirred
overnight at 60 °C. Then, the reaction was quenched with aqueous NaCl. A
whitish precipitate. The desired compound was isolated pure by filtration
in vacuo (400 mg, 67%). Mp: 188-190 °C. 1H NMR (200 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ
(ppm) 1.38 (s, 18H), 1.40 (s, 18H), 1.44 (s, 18H), 7.48 (s, 2H), 7.78 (s,
2H), 7.84 (s, 2H), 7.91 (s, 2H), 8.78 (s, 2H), 9.27 (s, 2H), 10.23 (s,
2H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ (ppm) 28.1 (CH3), 31.8 (2xCH3), 34.5
(2 × Cq), 111.2 (CH), 112.1 (CH), 114.8 (CH), 117.0 (CH), 122.9 (2 × Cq),
123.9 (Cq), 124.2 (Cq), 129.7 (Cq), 131,6 (Cq), 141.5 (2 × Cq), 153.2
(C=O), 153.7 (C=O). HRMS (ESI-TOF): m/z [M -H]-(C51H67N6O5) found
843.5179, calcd 843.5252.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bis(carbazolyl)ureas as Selective Receptors for the Recognition of
Hydrogenpyrophosphate in Aqueous Media
