$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B. A mixture of 7a-e (1.0 mmol) and
carbonyldiimdazole (CDI, 2.0 mmol) in THF (10 mL) was stirred at ambient
temperature for 4 h, followed by addition of the required amine (2.0
mmol) and heating to reflux for another 16 h. After cooling the reaction,
the mixture was evaporated and purified by silica gel column
chromatography.
1-(4-{2-[(5,6-Diphenylfuro[2,3-d]pyrimidin-4-yl)amino]-ethyl}phenyl)-3-(4-fluorophenyl)urea
24.17 Method B, using 7a and p-fluoro-aniline to give 24. Purification:
column chromatography over silica gel column using MeOH:CH2Cl2 (1:20).
Yield, 78%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.43 (s, 1H), 7.47-7.39 (m, 4H),
7.34-7.29 (m, 4H), 7.25-7.22 (m, 5H), 7.03-6.93 (m, 4H), 6.88 (s, 1H),
4.67 (t, J= 5.4 Hz, 1H), 3.69 (q, J= 6.0 Hz, 2H), 2.74 (t, J= 6.0 Hz,
2H). LCMS (ESI) m/z: 544 [M + H]+.
