$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of compound 4: Just before the reaction, BODIPY-B (120 mg, 0.24
mmol) was treated with hydrazine monohydrate (12 mg, 0.24 mmol) in
THF/MeOH (1:1, total 2mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 1h. The mixture was diluted by the addition of CH2Cl2 (20
mL) then washed with H2O (2 x 10 mL). The organic fraction was dried over
Na2SO4 then solvent was removed under reduced pressure. Orange solid as
BODIPY-B’. It was used directly in next step without further
purification. BODIPYB’ from last step was dissolved in MeOH (50mL) with
5-fdC (50 mg, 0.2 mmol) added. Following with several drops of glacial
acetic acid and p-anisidine (30 mg, 0.24 mmol) added. The reaction
mixture stayed at 50°C overnight. The mixture was evaporated in vacuo.
The crude product was purified by flash chromatography (SiO2, CHCl3-MeOH
= 10:1 as eluents). Orange solid as compound 6. A yield of 138 mg (95%)
was obtained. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ(ppm): 8.14(d, J = 12.6Hz, 2H),
8.00 (br, 1H), 7.50 (m, 2 H), 7.30 (m, 3 H), 6.10 (s, 2 H), 6.02(br, 1
H), 5.18-5.15(m, 3H), 4.97 (s, 1H), 4.12 (s, 1 H), 3.73 (s, 1H), 3.51(m,
2H), 2.37(s, 6H), 2.17(m, 1H), 1.93(m, 1H), 1.24 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (75
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ: 161.67, 154.73, 152.96, 147.50, 145.61, 142.57, 141.54,
138.61, 133.31, 130.51, 128.89, 127.64, 121.21, 98.13, 87.49, 85.49,
79.01, 74.65, 69.79, 60.85, 40.56, 14.04, 13.83. HRMS (ESI) calcd for
C30H33N6O5*BClF2 [M+Cl]- : 640.2304; found: 640.2322.
