$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of substituted phenyl semicarbazide (3a-b) Equimolar quantities
(0.05 mol) of substituted phenyl urea (2a-b) and hydrazine hydrate (AR
99-100 %) (2.5 ml, 0.05 mol) in ethanol were refluxed for 48 h with
stirring. The two-third volume of alcohol was distilled by vacuum
distillation and then poured into the crushed ice. The resultant
precipitate was filtered, washed with water, and dried. The solid mass
was recrystallized from 50 ml of absolute ethanol (Pandeya and Raja,
2002; Singhal and Paul, 2011). Compound 3a, yield 86%. Rfa: 0.64 ; Mp
(°C): 125 .
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and anticonvulsant evaluation of 2-(substituted
benzylidene/ethylidene)-N-(substituted phenyl)hydrazinecarboxamide
analogues
