$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: In a flame-dried Schlenk
tube under argon atmosphere, boronate 1 (100 mg, 0.415 mmol) and
triethylamine (116 mL, 0.829 mmol) were successively added to a stirred
suspension of polymer-supported phosphine (Novabiochem®, 1.7 mmol/g) (710
mg, 1.04 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (3 mL). The reaction mixture was cooled to 0°C.
A solution of tetrabromomethane (1.16 mmol, 385 mg) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was
added dropwise at 0°C. The reaction mixture was stirred at 0°C for 6
hours before the addition of the desired nucleophile (0.415 mmol). With
amino ester hydrochlorides, a second equivalent of triethylamine (0.415
mmol) was added before the nucleophile. The reaction mixture was stirred
at rt during 12h. Water (2 mL) was added and the aqueous layer was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 5 mL) .the combined organic layers were washed
with a saturated solution of NH4Cl, dried over MgSO4, filtrated and
concentrated under vacuo. The crude product was purified by silica gel
chromatography or flash chromatography, except for compound 4a which is
used without supplementary purification. (E)-Methyl
1-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)but-2-enylcarbamate 4a
(E)-1-Benzyl-3-(1-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)but-2-enyl)urea
4d Yield = 78% 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, δ ppm) 7.39-7.22 (m, 5H), 6.62 (br
s, 1H), 5.46 (dd, J = 15.6, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 5.30 (dq, J = 15.6, 6.0 Hz, 1H),
4.43-4.20 (m, 2H), 3.03 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 1.69-1.55 (m, 4H), 1.04 (s,
6H), 1.02 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, δ ppm) 163.1, 137.3, 132.4,
128.9, 128.0, 122.0, 80.1, 49.8, 45.4, 25.2, 24.7, 17.9. 11B NMR (96 MHz,
CDCl3, δ ppm) 22.4 (s), 12.4 (s). HRMS (ESI) calcd. for C18H27BN2O3Na
[M+Na]+ : 353.2012 found 353.2011. Column chromatography:
cyclohexane/EtOAc 50% to 100% (R f = 0.1, EtOAc/cylohexane 50/50).
