$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure (GP V) for Introducing
2-Urea.
1-(6-(2-Methoxyphenyl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)-3-(2-morpholinoethyl)urea
(10a) 6-(2-Methoxyphenyl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-amine (58 mg, 0.23 mmol) and
carbonyldiimidazole (112 mg, 0.679 mmol) was dissolved into anhydrous DMF
and stirred for 8 h at room temperature. 2-Morpholinoethanamine (150 μL,
1.13 mmol) was added. After the reaction finished, the resulting solution
was concentrated in vacuo. Then the crude mixture was purified with flash
column chromatography to give compound 10a
1-(6-(2-Ethoxyphenyl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)-3-(2-hydroxyethyl)-urea (10f)
Compound 10f was prepared according to GP V from
6-(2-ethoxyphenyl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-amine (32 mg, 0.11 mmol). (28 mg, 67%
yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, MeOH-d4) δ 1.29 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 3.41 (t, J
= 5.5 Hz, 2H), 3.69 (t, J = 5.5 Hz, 2H), 4.02 (q, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H),
6.95-7.05 (m, 2H), 7.23-7.33 (m, 2H), 7.52 (dd, J = 1.8, 8.4 Hz, 1H),
7.63 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.88 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
MeOH-d4) δ 15.1, 43.4, 61.9, 65.2, 114.0, 119.9, 122.0, 122.8, 129.0,
129.7, 131.7, 131.8, 132.4, 135.6, 149.0, 156.3, 157.2, 162.2. HRMS (EI+)
m/z calcd for C18H19N3O3S [M + Na]+, 380.1045; found, 380.1027.
