$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Benzimidazolone-2 (1). To a solution of urea (16.81 g, 0.28 mol) in of
glycol (200 mL) at room temperature was added o-phenylenediamine (27.02
g, 0.25 mol). After the mixture was stirred at 110 °C for 1 hour, then
stirred at 150 °C for another 7 hours. The mixture was cooled down to ∼40
°C, and about 100 mL of water were added with stirring for 20 min. The
precipitate was collected by suction filtration and washed by large
amounts of water, then washed by 100 mL 95% ethanol. The residue was
dried at 80 °C under vacuum. Yield: (23.46 g, 70%), pale solid. Melting
point is beyond 300 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ (ppm) 10.56 (s, 2H),
6.93 (s, 4H). IR (KBr, pellet, cm-1): 3137, 3031, 1739, 1483, 1362.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
