$DATUM 76
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-(1H-Benzo[d][1,2,3]triazol-6-yl)-3-(2-cyclohexylethyl)urea (4). To a
solution of 6-amino-1,2,3-benzotriazole (72 mg, 0.538 mmol) in DMF (2.0
mL) was added N,N'-carbonyldiimidazole (CDI; 106 mg, 0.654 mmol), and the
resulting mixture was stirred for 5 h at rt. Cyclohexylethylamine (109
mg, 0.861 mmol) was then added. After being stirred for 6 h at rt, the
resulting mixture was purified by preparative HPLC (50-100% methanol/0.1%
TFA in H2O).
1-(2-Cyclohexylethyl)-3-(2-oxo-2,3-dihydrobenzo[d]oxazol-6-yl)urea (7) as
a white solid, yield 138 mg, 76%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, d6-DMSO) δ 11.36 (s,
1H), 8.40 (s, 1H), 7.53 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.00-6.85 (m, 2H), 6.04 (t,
J = 5.6 Hz, 1H), 3.15-3.03 (m, 2H), 1.75-1.54 (m, 5H), 1.38-1.06 (m, 6H),
0.97-0.80 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, d6-DMSO) δ 155.7, 155.1, 143.89,
136.1, 124.4, 113.5, 109.9, 100.8, 37.7, 37.2, 35.0, 33.1 (two carbons),
26.6, 26.2 (two carbons); HPLC (method 1) 100%, tR 4.59 min; MS (ESI) m/z
304 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Exploiting an Allosteric Binding Site of PRMT3 Yields Potent and
Selective Inhibitors
