$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-(1H-Benzo[d][1,2,3]triazol-6-yl)-3-(2-cyclohexylethyl)urea (4). To a
solution of 6-amino-1,2,3-benzotriazole (72 mg, 0.538 mmol) in DMF (2.0
mL) was added N,N'-carbonyldiimidazole (CDI; 106 mg, 0.654 mmol), and the
resulting mixture was stirred for 5 h at rt. Cyclohexylethylamine (109
mg, 0.861 mmol) was then added. After being stirred for 6 h at rt, the
resulting mixture was purified by preparative HPLC (50-100% methanol/0.1%
TFA in H2O).
1-(Benzo[d][1,2,3]thiadiazol-6-yl)-3-(2-(2-fluorophenyl)-2-hydroxyethyl)urea
(20) as a white solid, yield 57 mg, 54%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, d4-MeOH) δ
8.45-8.37 (m, 2H), 7.58 (td, J = 7.5, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.46 (dd, J = 9.0, 2.0
Hz, 1H), 7.29 (tdd, J = 7.3, 5.3, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.19 (td, J = 7.5, 0.8 Hz,
1H), 7.06 (ddd, J = 10.5, 8.2, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 5.13 (dd, J = 7.3, 4.5 Hz,
1H), 3.60 (dd, J = 13.7, 4.5 Hz, 1H), 3.44 (dd, J = 13.7, 7.4 Hz, 1H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, d4-MeOH) δ 159.9 (d, J = 244.4 Hz), 156.14, 153.88,
142.65, 141.60, 129.4 (d, J = 13.7 Hz), 128.9 (d, J = 8.3 Hz), 127.5 (d,
J = 4.4 Hz), 124.0 (d, J = 3.5 Hz), 123.1, 119.2, 114.7 (d, J = 22.0 Hz),
105.4, 66.4, 45.6; HPLC (method 1) 100%, tR 3.26 min; MS (ESI) m/z 333 [M
+ H]+.
