$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 5.1.3. General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Ureas 62−75. A solution of substituted anilines (10.0 mmol) dissolved in
THF (80 mL) was slowly dripped into a stirred solution of triphosgene
(2.98 g, 10.0 mmol) in THF (10 mL) by using a constant-pressure dropping
funnel. NEt3 (3 mL, 21.0 mmol) was then added slowly to the reaction
mixture after the anilines were added. After evaporation of the solvent,
the residue was taken up in THF (80 mL), and 4-aminophenol (0.93 g, 8.5
mmol) was added directly to the residue. The reaction mixture was stirred
at 45 °C for 2 h, and the solvent was subsequently removed in vacuo. The
residue obtained was dissolved in acetone (4 mL), and upon addition of
water, a solid precipitated. This solid was collected, washed with water
and Et2O, and dried under vacuum to give the products 62−75. 73, yield
(64−99%)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
