$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B: A solution of
6-(aminooxy)-N-(benzyloxy)hexanamide 23 (1 equiv.) in dry CH2Cl2 (2 mL)
was added dropwise to a suspension of CDT (1.15 equiv.) in in dry CH2Cl2
(5 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred for 2 h at room temperature.
Afterward, the respective amine (1 equiv.) and triethylamine (3 drops)
were added and the reaction mixture was stirred over night and
subsequently evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue was dissolved
in ethyl acetate (20 mL) and the solution was extracted with a saturated
solution of NaHCO3 (3 x 5 mL), water (5 mL), 1 M HCl (5 mL), water (5
mL), dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue
was purified by column chromatography using ethyl acetate or ethyl
acetate:methanol (9:1) as eluent.
N-(Benzyloxy)-6-((3-(4-isopropylphenyl)ureido)oxy)hexanamide (11g).
Prepared according to method B. Yellow solid; yield 67%. mp 109 °C. 1H
NMR (500.13 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 1.17 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 6H), 1.24-1.34 (m,
2H), 1.50-1.66 (m, 4H), 1.97 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 2.79-2.86 (m, 1H), 3.74
(t, J = 6.7 Hz, 2H), 4.78 (s, 2H), 7.12 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.31-7.43
(m, 5H), 7.46 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 8.57 (s, 1H), 9.37 (s, 1H), 10.96 (s,
1H) ppm. 13C NMR (125.76 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 23.91, 24.64, 24.72, 27.13,
32.06, 32.70, 75.51, 76.66, 119.65, 126.04, 128.08, 128.17, 128.65,
135.99, 136.56, 142.41, 157.09, 169.19 ppm. IR (KBr): ν̃ =3318, 3208
(NH), 2956, 2867 (CH2), 1660 (C=O) cm-1. Anal. Calcd. for C23H31N3O4: C
66.81, H 7.56, N 10.16. Found: C 66.77, H 7.42, N 10.30.
