$DATUM Alternatively, 2a was synthesised by dissolving S2 (460 mg, 2.15 mmol, 1
equiv.) in CH2Cl2 (0.2 M) and adding Et3N (1.5 equiv.) and p-chlorophenyl
isocyanate (1 equiv.). After stirring for 24 h at r.t. to the mixture NaH
(5 equiv.) and MeI (5 equiv.) were sequentially added at 0 °C. The
reaction was stirred for 24 h at r.t., quenched with methanol and NH4Cl
(sat. sol.) and then extracted with EtOAc. The organic phases were
combined, dried over MgSO4, concentrated under reduced pressure and
purified by flash column chromatography (SiO2, Petrol/EtOAc : 9/1 + 1%
Et3N) to give the desired urea 2a. 2a (583 mg, 75%) IR νmax (CHCl3)/cm-1:
2963, 1641, 1489; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.32-7.15 (m, 7H), 6.95-6.89
(m, 2H), 5.35 (dd, J=8.8, 7.1 , 1H), 3.15 (s, 3H), 2.26 (s, 3H),
1.92-1.81 (m, 1H), 1.77-1.67 (m, 1H) 1.35-1.17 (m, 6H), 0.86 (t, J=6.9 ,
3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 162.0, 145.6, 139.9, 129.6, 129.4,
128.3, 127.8, 127.3, 125.2, 58.5, 40.1, 31.7, 30.8, 30.3, 26.4, 22.6,
14.0; HRMS (ESI): calcd for C21H27N2OClNa (M+Na+) 381.1704, found
381.1710
